{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings"]]},"metadata":{"title":"SelectiveSemiring","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Semiring.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Semirings\/Semiring.swift#L74"},"modules":[{"name":"Semirings"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SelectiveSemiring","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","externalID":"s:9Semirings17SelectiveSemiringP","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SelectiveSemiring"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"protocol"},"abstract":[{"text":"A semiring whose ⊕ returns one of its operands (a selective dioid in Gondran–Minoux’s terms),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with ","type":"text"},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as its natural order.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/semirings\/selectivesemiring"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/SelectiveSemiring","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SelectiveSemiring"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9Semirings8SemiringP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Semiring","identifier":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a < b"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊕ b == a"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a != b"},{"type":"text","text":", read as “a is better than b”. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a ⊕ b"},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"better of the two, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"type":"text","text":" is a strict total order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"zero"},{"type":"text","text":" is the worst element. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<"},{"type":"text","text":" is not the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order of the raw values: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BottleneckSemiring(9) < BottleneckSemiring(2)"},{"type":"text","text":" because wider is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"better, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BooleanSemiring(true) < BooleanSemiring(false)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Dijkstra’s algorithm, Bellman–Ford, DAG shortest paths and Floyd–Warshall in ShortestPaths take","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a selective semiring. Dijkstra’s algorithm also needs every examined weight to be no better than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"one"},{"text":", so that extending a path never improves it. A negative tropical weight breaks that, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no bottleneck or Boolean weight does.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships","title":"Inherits From","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/Semiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SL","doc:\/\/Semirings\/SQ"]},{"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BooleanSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/BottleneckSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/MaxPlusSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/TropicalSemiring","doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/ViterbiSemiring"]}],"references":{"doc://Semirings/documentation/Semirings/MaxPlusSemiring":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The max-plus semiring (max, +) over "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Value"},{"type":"text","text":", for longest paths, also called the arctic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"semiring."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaxPlusSemiring"}],"title":"MaxPlusSemiring","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/semirings\/maxplussemiring","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaxPlusSemiring"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/MaxPlusSemiring"},"doc://Semirings/documentation/Semirings/LexicographicSemiring":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings\/LexicographicSemiring","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/semirings\/lexicographicsemiring","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographic product of two selective semirings, for paths best by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"First"},{"type":"text","text":" with ties"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"broken by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Second"},{"text":" (Mohri’s lexicographic semiring): the shortest among the widest paths, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the fewest hops among the shortest.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LexicographicSemiring","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LexicographicSemiring","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"LexicographicSemiring"},"doc://Semirings/documentation/Semirings":{"url":"\/documentation\/semirings","title":"Semirings","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Semirings\/documentation\/Semirings","role":"collection","abstract":[